in death stranding there are plenty of  human enemies out in the world that can  instantly ruin your day so we've  compiled a guide to give you the edge  while taking them on mules are the first  type of human enemies you can encounter  this band of troublemakers attacked  Porter's on-site and live for the high  of stealing and hoarding cargo however  their main perogative isn't killing  think post-apocalyptic team rocket mule  camps are always surrounded by a  proximity fence that's triggered when  you pass their borders there are a few  quirks to this fence though the main  trigger is cargo so if you're not  carrying delivery cargo for an order you  will not appear in their skin which  makes it easier to enter without being  seen once you obtain the sensor  Nullification skill for your odor deck  from the time fall form you can time  your sensor scan to cancel their ping to  sneak in undetected past their fences  once you get past their borders you need  to start strategizing a way to whittle  down their numbers use the odor duck  scanner and the environment around you  to sneak into their camp take cover  behind rocks or in tall grass and scout  out their positions and then take them  down one by one by using the strange  from behind you can incapacitate them  you can also use the bola gun to tie  them down from a distance  they'll keep in mind it may alert others  nearby if you want to get loud there are  many ways to take down mules in early  hours you don't have much equipment to  deal with them besides your fists and  your strand so it's usually not  recommended to run into mules until you  get some better gear to use the strand  hold l2 to ready yourself and hit or two  to parry physical attacks the timing is  lenient so don't worry about precise  timing but make sure that you're facing  your attacker also it takes a second to  ready yourself for the parry so give  yourself enough time to get into  position while you can instant ko a mule  by binding them with a strand you are  left open to attack during this  animation so be careful it's also  possible to dodge attacks with nothing  equipped in your hands hold r2 or l2 and  then jump to dodge use this to counter  attack enemies and hit them from behind  in an absolute pinch you can also rely  on the hematocrit aids you picked up in  chapter 2 to stun enemies as well even  though it says are designed for BTS if  you're not too worried about collecting  the materials that the Mules drop you  can also use it against them  you can pick up dropped cargo by holding  l2 or r2 over it and do a powerful melee  attack with a square but you can also  throw it back by releasing l2 or r2 in  the middle of your melee swing try not  to do this with your own precious cargo  as a contents get heavily damaged both  punching and straining mules are great  ways to take them down but they're both  slow and if you're being attacked by  multiple enemies it's usually a recipe  for disaster  generally try not to get into this mosh  pit situation in the first place as the  worst thing to do is fight a whole gang  at once and a one-on-one fight these  enemies pose little threat but as more  and more their friends arrive that's  when the situation starts getting out of  control especially when they're shocked  Spears are raining down on you later in  Chapter 3 you'll get access to much more  fun equipment to take on mules such as  decoys bola guns and special grenades  vog and smoke decoys are useful to start  the fight off with as it's pinged as  fake cargo it's best to drop it right  where the ping location is and relocate  somewhere else  enemies will pick the decoy and set it  off as a trap bola guns are fairly  straightforward holding the trigger down  will widen the bola shot and make it  much easier to hit your targets this is  a great weapon to make sure you're not  taking too many on at once make sure you  kick a tied mule so they don't come back  to bite you later if you can afford to  try to go for the headshot  this will wrap around their neck and  knock them out instantly rather than a  body shot where they'll be temporarily  tied down instead smoke grenades are  great for crowd control as enemies  caught in a smoke will be temporarily  stunned and will cough uncontrollably  any smoked enemies are also findable the  best uses for defense use it when you're  surrounded and escape as it doesn't  affect yourself stun grenades as  advertised stun enemies but more  importantly vehicles use one to stun  multiple enemies off a truck and disable  the vehicle temporarily for most stun  grenades are also great and are sticky  so attach them to enemies and goodies  and have some fun careful not to be  caught in your own blast though  probably the most underrated weapon of  all is a sticky gun  this weapon rips cargo right off of  meals and brings it to you on a hook  shot hold down our chew or else you to  catch stolen cargo and throw it right  back they shot it at an enemy it will  turn them around for you perfect for you  to do a nice takedown it also has a ton  of ammo so it's a worthwhile gun to  fabricate starting in episode 4 you'll  start running into a new faction  terrorists these dangerous foes are far  more bloodthirsty and strategic than  mules and most importantly they carry  real guns in this case you'll now have  to start thinking about equipping armor  and blood packs and putting those cryo  bites you've been collecting the use but  for the most part the strategy it takes  to overcome them as similar to mules  previous tactics using knockout  equipment still come into play here but  by this point in the game you'll also  have access to guns as well make sure to  get non lethal rubber rounds or else  with real guns you'll have a lot of  cleaning up to do after make sure to  check out our other video explaining why  real guns can be a problem  make sure to sneak up in as many  terrorists as you can before turning on  the fire use a non lethal assault rifle  a long-range and the riot shotgun a  short-range if you can afford to without  exposing yourself too much use a ride  shotguns small stunt to close a gap and  then take them down to save some ammo  take cover keep scanning and take the  high ground to come out on top  ultimately once you take down a whole  mule or terrorist encampment you'll be  rewarded with free rein to all of their  useful cargo we know during your journey  you don't always have the luxury to keep  all this nifty equipment on you so pick  and choose your equipment and your  battles wisely hopefully this guy will  keep you on top of the battle and for  more deaths training guides and content  keep it here on gamespot  you
 

